  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Saint Joseph’s University is a private Jesuit institution that has been providing a rigorous liberal arts education for over 170 years. Known for its \"whole-person\" approach to education, the university fosters intellectual and spiritual growth across more than 260 academic programmes. Whether you are interested in business, healthcare, or the arts, you will find a supportive community that emphasizes both professional success and social responsibility.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>Life at Saint Joseph’s is vibrant and inclusive. You can join a variety of student clubs and organizations that cater to diverse interests, from academic societies to cultural groups. The university's Jesuit values promote a welcoming environment where you can engage in community service, leadership development, and campus-wide events that celebrate the student body’s 44 represented nations.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>You have several on-campus housing options that offer a safe and convenient living environment. From traditional residence halls to suite-style apartments, the university provides spaces designed to help you transition into college life. For those seeking budget-friendly options outside of the university grounds, there are various off-campus apartments located in the nearby suburban and city areas.</p><p>If you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to <a href=\"https://onelink.to/jb48ev\">download our app</a> and check out the <a href=\"https://edvoy.com/student/stays\">Stays</a> feature!</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<ol><li><strong>Library</strong><ul><li>The <strong>Post Learning Commons and Drexel Library</strong> serve as your central hub for research and collaboration. You will find extensive digital databases, quiet study zones, and the <strong>Wachterhauser Seminar Room</strong> for group projects.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Sports</strong><ul><li>You can stay active through the university’s fitness centres, intramural sports, and NCAA Division I athletic programmes. The campus features modern playing fields and gym facilities for both competitive and recreational use.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Laboratories</strong><ul><li>The university boasts high-tech facilities such as the <strong>Center for Excellence in Practice</strong>, a 20,000-square-foot clinical simulation lab in Lancaster, and specialized science labs for hands-on research.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Cafeteria</strong><ul><li>There are multiple dining options on campus, ranging from full-service dining halls to quick cafes. You can enjoy a variety of cuisines that cater to different dietary needs and preferences.</li></ul></li></ol>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Campuses",
      "value": "<p><strong>Hawk Hill (Main Campus)</strong> Located on the edge of Philadelphia and Lower Merion Township, this 125-acre campus offers a mix of city energy and suburban charm. It is the primary home for undergraduate students and central administrative facilities.</p><p><strong>University City</strong> Situated in West Philadelphia, this location is the hub for graduate health professions and pharmaceutical sciences. You can easily travel between Hawk Hill and University City via a dedicated shuttle service.</p><p><strong>Lancaster</strong> This campus focuses on nursing and allied health programs. It provides a unique urban-rural blend in South Central Pennsylvania, featuring advanced simulation technology for healthcare students.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
